            "lens": "review-risk",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 29 changed paths for security, authorization, data exposure and unsafe input handling.",
              "The new SessionStart hook and the 'memory plan --instructions' command are read-only. They write no binding and no log, and they fail silent or exit 2 on error. The SessionStart path swallows panics and reads stdin through a bounded reader.",
              "The gate-task change appends the instructions block to sub-agent prompts. The block is derived from local workflow state, not from attacker-controlled input. Hook input is size-bounded by the existing stdinSizeLimit. The rewrite never denies a call, and a panic in the instruction lookup yields an empty block.",
              "The gate-task rewrite now answers with the instructions block even when the contract file is unreadable. This is a deliberate fail-safe that still never blocks, and it adds no exposure.",
              "The appendInstructions change in engine/gate/gate.go now requires the block to end the prompt. This removes a bypass in which a prompt could quote the block and avoid receiving it. It is a hardening, not a regression.",
              "The memory-plan skill ships with an .approval.json, a registry entry and a manifest entry. They add no executable code and no secrets, and no dependency or lockfile changed.",
              "No reachable exploit, secret exposure, or dependency vulnerability was found that this candidate caused."
            ]
          }
        }
