            "lens": "review-resilience",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "The new hook paths fail safe. boundInstructions in engine/cmd/binding_wiring.go recovers from panics and returns an empty block. sessionStart in engine/cmd/projection_hook.go stays silent on any read, decode or encode failure, and it never writes.",
              "gate-task in engine/cmd/gate_task.go still exits 0 with a pass-through when the contract is missing or unreadable, or when stdin cannot be read. The instructions block is added only when a workflow is bound. The embedded-contract entry is forced to nil instructions, so the two parallel Agent hooks cannot race to rewrite the same call.",
              "appendInstructions in engine/gate/gate.go stays idempotent: it uses a suffix check on the right-trimmed prompt, so re-running the rewrite does not append the block twice.",
              "The one changed gate-task stderr warning (--contract-file missing) is a diagnostic only. Stdout and exit status are unchanged, and the golden files were updated with it. I found no concrete failure or measured impact."
            ]
          }
        }
