            "lens": "review-reliability",
            "findings": [],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 29 changed paths. I found no reliability defect that this candidate introduced.",
              "gate-task: every unmanaged path (no contract file, an unreadable contract, an unknown embedded name) now goes through agentGateAnswer with an empty config. With no binding, that returns the pass-through `{}`. This is covered by TestGateTaskWithoutABindingAnswersAsBefore.",
              "The embedded-contract entry sets instructions to nil, so only the --contract-file entry rewrites the call. TestGateTaskWithAnEmbeddedContractNeverAppendsTheInstructions proves this.",
              "boundInstructions recovers from panics and returns an empty block, so the hooks cannot fail the call they serve. sessionStart is silent on every error path and never writes. TestSessionStartIsSilentWithoutAWorkflowToFollow covers this and checks that the binding of a closed workflow is kept.",
              "The appendInstructions change (HasSuffix on the trimmed prompt) is idempotent for a prompt that already ends with the block. A new test covers the case where the block is quoted mid-prompt.",
              "memory plan --instructions: parse-time rejection of the profile-form flags, exit 2 on refusal, and exit 0 with a message when nothing is bound are all asserted. The JSON plan without --instructions is still asserted in the existing test path.",
